def get_age_group(age):
    if age < 1 or age > 120:
        return "Error: Age must be between 1 and 120."
    elif age < 13:
        return "child"
    elif age < 20:
        return "teenager"
    elif age < 65:
        return "adult"
    else:
        return "senior"

def main():
    name = input("Enter your full name: ")
    name = name.title()  # convert to title case
    age = int(input("Enter your age: "))

    group = get_age_group(age)

    if group == "Error":
        print(group)
    else:
        print(f"{name} is a {group}.")

if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
```

This program defines two functions: `get_age_group()` which validates the age and returns the appropriate age group based on the age range, and `main()` which gets user input, calls `get_age_group()`, and prints the result. The program handles errors by returning an error message if the age is not within the valid range.
